 2067/ CCC :                            ; 12x16 fixed-point multiply
 2068/ CCC :                            ; Formula: R10:R11 = R8:R9 * COEFF / 2048
 2069/ CCC :                            ; COEFF is 1.11 fixed-point (1 integer bit, 11 fractional bits):
 2070/ CCC :                            ;   bit 11 (PITCH_HI bit 3) = integer bit (weight x1.0)
 2071/ CCC :                            ;   bits 10:0 = fractional (weight x0.0 to x0.999)
 2072/ CCC :                            ;   Range: 0.0 to ~2.0.  Unity (x1.0) at COEFF=$800
 2073/ CCC :                            ; PITCH_HI[5:4] = EXSLA staging (not used by multiply)
 2074/ CCC :                            ; PITCH_HI[7:6] = EXSLA bits (used by pitch_acc_positive AFTER multiply)
 2075/ CCC :                            ; 12 unrolled iterations: 8 from PITCH_LO + 4 from PITCH_HI[3:0]
 2076/ CCC :                            ; NOTE: no final RRC after last iteration -> bit 11 has weight 1.0
 2077/ CCC :                            ; When COEFF > $800 (multiplier > 1.0): result can exceed ACC
 2078/ CCC :                            ;   -> carry after last ADC -> JP C, overflow
